   <refbody>    <section>
      <p>This section describes the API authentication process.</p>
      <p>OAuth 2.0 client credentials allow connection with the ADI OtoSense™ SMS REST API, created for machine-to-machine authentication.</p>
      <p>OAuth authentication requires the following steps:</p>
      <ol>
    <li><xref href="../access_the_api/create_a_client_api_key.dita" format="dita">Create a Client API Key</xref>.</li>
    <li><xref href="../access_the_api/generate_a_token.dita" format="dita">Generate a Token</xref>.</li>
    <li><xref href="../access_the_api/make_authenticated_requests.dita" format="dita">Make Authenticated Requests</xref>.</li>
    </ol>
    </section>
<section>
      <title>Result</title>
      <note type="note">Note:</note>
         <p>Analog Devices recommends a least-privileged approach to API users. Ensure you assign roles with the least privilege level to all API users.</p>
    </section></refbody>
